speechtext:
Order, please. I have the honour to inform the House that when the House went up to the Senate Chamber the Deputy Governor General had been pleased to give in Her Majesty's name the Royal Assent to the following bills:
Bill C-129, An Act to amend the Bretton Woods Agreements Act and the International Development Association Act-Chapter No. 12S;
Bill C-90, An Act to amend the Customs Tariff and to repeal certain Acts in consequence thereof-Chapter No. 129;
Bill C-135, An Act to amend the National Housing Act (No. 2)-Chapter No. 130;
Bill C-134, An Act respecting rebates of interest on farm loans made under the Farm Credit Act-Chapter No. 131;
Bill C-140, An Act for granting to Her Majesty certain sums of money for the Government of Canada for the financial year ending the 31st March, 1983- Chapter No. 132.
Time Allocation
It being six o'clock, I do now leave the chair until 8 p.m. At 6.08 p.m. the House took recess.
